[{"title":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"","category":"page","text":"CurrentModule = MetropolisHastingsMCMC"},{"title":"MetropolisHastingsMCMC.jl","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"#MetropolisHastingsMCMC.jl","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"","category":"page","text":"MetropolisHastingsMCMC.jl provides a lightweight adaptive random-walk Metropolis–Hastings sampler. It keeps the convenient LogDensityProblems.jl interface used by the Barker sampler while dropping the gradient requirement."},{"title":"Quick start","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"#Quick-start","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"LogDensityProblems.jl targets","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"#LogDensityProblems.jl-targets","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"","category":"page","text":"using MetropolisHastingsMCMC\nusing TransformVariables: transform, inverse, as, asℝ, asℝ₊\nusing TransformedLogDensities: TransformedLogDensity\nusing LogDensityProblemsAD: ADgradient\nusing Distributions\n\nx = rand(10)\ny = 2 .+ 1.5x .+ randn(10) * 0.2\n\nmodel(x, θ) = θ.a + θ.b * x\n\nfunction likelihood(θ, x, y)\n    sum(logpdf(Normal(model(x[i], θ), θ.σ), y[i]) for i in eachindex(y))\nend\n\nprior(θ) = logpdf(Normal(0, 1), θ.a) +\n           logpdf(Normal(0, 1), θ.b) +\n           logpdf(Exponential(1), θ.σ)\n\nposterior(θ, x, y) = likelihood(θ, x, y) + prior(θ)\n\ntrans = as((a = asℝ, b = asℝ, σ = asℝ₊))\nlp = ADgradient(:ForwardDiff, TransformedLogDensity(trans, θ -> posterior(θ, x, y)))\n\ninits = inverse(trans, (a = 0.0, b = 0.0, σ = 0.5))\nresults = mh_mcmc(lp, inits; n_iter = 5_000)\n\ntransform.(Ref(trans), eachrow(results.samples))  # samples in the original parameterisation"},{"title":"Direct log-density functions","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"#Direct-log-density-functions","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"","category":"page","text":"using MetropolisHastingsMCMC\n\nbanana(x) = -0.05 * (100 * (x[2] - x[1]^2)^2 + (1 - x[1])^2)\n\nres = mh_mcmc(banana, [5.0, -5.0]; n_iter = 2_000)\nres.samples\nres.log_p"},{"title":"API reference","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"#API-reference","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"","category":"page","text":"mh_mcmc"},{"title":"MetropolisHastingsMCMC.mh_mcmc","page":"Metropolis-Hastings MCMC","location":"#MetropolisHastingsMCMC.mh_mcmc","category":"function","text":"mh_mcmc(lp, inits; n_iter, σ, target_acceptance_rate, κ, n_iter_adaptation, rng)\n\nAdaptive random-walk Metropolis–Hastings sampler. Works with targets implementing the LogDensityProblems.jl interface or plain log-density functions.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nn_iter::Integer = 100: number of MCMC iterations.\nσ::Real = 2.4 / (length(inits)^(1 / 6)): initial global scale of the random-walk proposal.\ntarget_acceptance_rate::Real = 0.234: desired acceptance rate guiding adaptation.\nκ::Real = 0.6: exponent of the Robbins–Monro learning rate, must be in (0.5, 1].\nn_iter_adaptation: number of iterations during which adaptation is active (default Inf).\nrng::AbstractRNG = default_rng(): RNG used for proposals and acceptance decisions.\n\nReturns\n\nNamed tuple with fields\n\nsamples: matrix of size (n_iter, dimension) containing the Markov chain.\nlog_p: vector with the log-density evaluations.\n\n\n\n\n\n"}]
